    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0253" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg253"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr.
                            Dayton</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 23, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 29th of August (No.
                    37) was duly received.</p>
                <p>The proceedings it relates had, however, been anticipated, and it only remains to
                    be said in regard to them, that your conduct therein is fully approved</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William. L. Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
